---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContactBand from "../../components/ContactBand.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="SSI Help in Illinois | Williams & Swee, Ltd." description="Plain-language information about Supplemental Security Income and how Williams & Swee, Ltd. helps with SSI claims." path="ssi/">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="section section-narrow"><p class="breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a> / SSI</p><p class="eyebrow">Supplemental Security Income</p><h1>Help with an SSI claim</h1><p class="lede">SSI may help some people who have a disability and limited income and resources.</p></div></header>
  <div class="section section-narrow">
    <h2>What is SSI?</h2>
    <p>SSI stands for Supplemental Security Income. It is a federal program run by the Social Security Administration.</p>
    <p>You do not need the same work history required for SSDI. Social Security also looks at your income, resources, living situation, and disability.</p>
    <h2>You may need to show</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list"><li>How your health condition limits daily activities.</li><li>How your condition affects your ability to work.</li><li>Information about your income and resources.</li><li>Medical information that supports your claim.</li></ul>
    <div class="callout"><strong>This page gives general information.</strong> SSI rules change and every situation is different. An attorney should review the final production wording.</div>
    <h2>How the firm may help</h2>
    <p>Williams &amp; Swee, Ltd. can review where you are in the process, help gather information, and explain possible next steps.</p>
    <p>Last reviewed for demo: July 29, 2026. Source: <a href="https://www.ssa.gov/ssi">Social Security Administration SSI information</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <ContactBand heading="Questions about an SSI claim?" />
</BaseLayout>
